    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and all four ops requirements are met. The existing test passes. I also checked it end to end with a stub transport whose first response is a 500, so the SDK had to retry once: both attempts were logged on `app.http` as `GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models`, and each request carried the 5s connect / 30s read, write and pool timeouts.\n\n```python\nTIMEOUT = httpx2.Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)\nMAX_RETRIES = 2\n\ndef _log_request(request: httpx2.Request) -> None:\n    logger.info(\"%s %s\", request.method, request.url)\n\ndef build_client(api_key: str, transport=None) -> OpenAI:\n    http_client = DefaultHttpxClient(\n        timeout=TIMEOUT,\n        transport=transport,\n        event_hooks={\"request\": [_log_request]},\n    )\n    return OpenAI(api_key=api_key, timeout=TIMEOUT, max_retries=MAX_RETRIES, http_client=http_client)\n```\n\nTwo things about the pinned `openai==3.19.2` that shaped this:\n\n- **It uses `httpx2`, not `httpx`.** The client and the stub transports the tests pass in must be `httpx2` objects. An `httpx.MockTransport` won't work.\n- **The SDK sets its own timeout on every request.** A timeout set only on the HTTP client is ignored if it happens to equal the library's default, so I pass it to both `OpenAI(...)` and the HTTP client.\n\nThe client is built with the SDK's `DefaultHttpxClient` so it keeps the SDK's connection limits and redirect settings. A request hook runs on every attempt, including retries, which is why each retry is logged.\n\nI couldn't delete my scratch script `check_client_tmp.py` from the project root because the removal needed approval, so please delete it yourself. I didn't add or change any dependencies."
